Generate the autocompletion script for
the fish shell.

To load completions in your current
shell session:

        cron-person completion fish |
        source

To load completions for every new
session, execute once:

        cron-person completion fish >
        ~/.config/fish/completions/cron-person.fish

You will need to start a new shell for
this setup to take effect.

Usage:
  cron-person completion fish [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help
        help for fish
      --no-descriptions
        disable completion descriptions

Global Flags:
      --config string
        Path to custom configuration
        file (default:
        $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cron-person/config.json)
      --store string
        Path to custom authorization
        state file (default:
        $XDG_STATE_HOME/cron-person/allowed.json)
